# README

This script updates the HTML redirect files in GCS (`latest/` subfolders) for every ISiK IG
module so that they point to the highest semver-versioned folder currently published.

## Prerequisites

- [Google Cloud SDK](https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install) (`gcloud`, `gsutil`)
- Bash (Linux, macOS, or WSL on Windows)
- Authenticated session: `gcloud auth login`

## Usage

```bash
# Auto-detect latest version in dev (default)
./update-ig-redirect.sh

# Explicitly set version, target qs environment
./update-ig-redirect.sh --version 6.0.0 --realm qs

# Preview what would happen without writing anything to GCS
./update-ig-redirect.sh --dry-run --realm prod
```

## Parameters

| Parameter | Default | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `--version` | `latest` | Target version string (e.g. `6.0.0`, `6.0.0-rc1`). When `latest`, the script auto-detects the highest semver folder in each module. |
| `--realm` | `dev` | Target environment. One of `dev`, `qs`, `prod`. |
| `--dry-run` | *(flag)* | Print gsutil write commands without executing them. GCS reads still run (for version detection). |

## Realm → Bucket mapping

| Realm | GCS Bucket |
|-------|-----------|
| `dev` | `gematik_gemspec_fhir_dev-0` |
| `qs`  | `gematik_gemspec_fhir_qs-0` |
| `prod`| `gematik_gemspec_fhir_prod-0` |

Base path within each bucket: `ig/fhir/isik/`

## Context

The ISiK IGs are published via the gematik GCS:
https://console.cloud.google.com/storage/browser/gematik_gemspec_fhir_dev-0/ig/fhir/isik

Within every IG module folder (e.g. `basis`, `dokumentenaustausch`) there is a `latest/`
subfolder containing HTML redirect files. Each file performs a client-side redirect to the
corresponding page in the current versioned folder.

## How it works

1. Lists all module folders under `gs://<bucket>/ig/fhir/isik/`.
2. For each module, identifies all versioned sub-folders (e.g. `6.0.0`, `5.2.1-rc2`) and
   picks the highest one using semver ordering (`sort -V`).
3. Lists all `*.html` files under `<module>/latest/`.
   - If no `latest/` folder exists for a module, a notice is logged and the module is skipped.
4. Downloads each HTML file, replaces the old version string in the `<meta refresh>` and
   `<link rel="canonical">` tags, and uploads the file back to GCS.

